      "side": 0,
      "message": "\u003e Did the crash happen with AVX2 or AVX512, in highbd or 8-bit mode? And does chromium call VP9_SET_BYTE_ALIGNMENT at any place?\n\nThere wasn\u0027t a crash in AVX2 or AVX512 (I suspected those first). Instead there was a decode mismatch, which I wasn\u0027t able to reproduce with `vpxdec`:\n\n```\nthird_party/blink/tools/run_web_tests.py --debug \\\n  --no-show-results --nocheck-sys-deps \\\n  --no-retry-failures media/video-colorspace-yuv422.html\n...\n[1/1] media/video-colorspace-yuv422.html failed unexpectedly (image diff) 1.1559s\n```\n\nChrome uses external frame buffers, but all of the calculations should be hidden from it. Changing `VP9_DEC_BORDER_IN_PIXELS` back to `32` and removing the alignment check in yv12config.c fixes the test.",
      "parentUuid": "96c81c7c_45f3bff3",
